ual gameplay the nice thing the  x-wing has is it's got all three systems  it's got its engines it's got its  lasers and it's got shields you can  shift those double front or behind you  which is something you know we've heard  in the films  but then the tie fighters canonically  don't have shields at all  she said okay what do we do to make that  fair to get to kind of balance these two  ships out but have similar roles but are  on opposite factions and we need to keep  uh  more or less lined up if you fly the two  in our game the x-wing feels a bit  heavier it's got a bit more substance to  it  the tie fighter has zippier turns it's  just a faster ship and a more easily  maneuverable ship and so that helps kind  of counterbalance the shields in and of  itself  but the ability to control the shields  to put them to front or back  is giving another edge to the x-wing so  how do we counter that  what we do is we use the same buttons  that we would use for shield control on  an x-wing  on its high fighter and some of the  other ties we use that for emergency  power conversion  which is the ability to pull all the  juice out of your engines and dump them  into your lasers  or vice versa on the fly so you can  quickly get out of trouble or quickly  juice up your weapons for a massive  attack  in a hurry in a way that the rebel ships  can't some of the things we we had to do  for the x-wing were  changing the viewport kind of slimming  down the struts a bit  it's a bunch of invisible changes that  make it feel like the movie i had to  take the existing dashboard and you know  its angular shape and how how high it is  that's iconic so we obviously had to  have that  we panned and scaled and kind of moved  around to create additional room  so we'd be able to fit all the gameplay  components for each of these  changes basically it's a slide in the  deck showing the original  showing the intended change and  justifying why but  any change we were doing you know using  the ma